5201: and \ref{prop:source-interface-record-file-consistency} identify the same
5202: interface by pinned commit, JSON mirror, and bundled source snapshot.  Hence the
5203: discovery-gate hypotheses of the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface} are
5204: not supplied by free prose; they are supplied, at the bounded source-interface
5205: level, by recorded paths and record files in $P$.  Proposition~\ref{prop:current-package-acceptance-certificate-ledger}
5206: adds the submission-local acceptance entries for these premises: the imported
5207: source-interface claim is entry $a_1$, and the route/submission package claim is
5208: entry $a_2$.
5209: 
5210: For the case-study claims, Lemma~\ref{lem:gate-witness-criterion} states that a
5211: record naming the source or artifact surface, failed invariant, gate decision,
5212: and safe manuscript lesson is a path-verified safety-interface witness and not a
5213: command-run witness unless the extra command-run fields are recorded.
5214: Proposition~\ref{prop:path-complete-case-witnesses} applies this criterion to
5215: the four case kinds used in the paper: promotion, route overlap, theorem-content
5216: growth, and artifact limitation.  Thus the rows later displayed in
5217: Table~\ref{tab:case-witnesses}, together with the manifest file named in $P$,
5218: provide passable path-verified evidence surfaces for exactly those bounded case
5219: claims.  Proposition~\ref{prop:current-package-acceptance-certificate-ledger}
5220: identifies these four case-study claims with entries $a_3$--$a_6$ and records
5221: their fields $K$, $\ell$, $E$, $H$, $R$, $D$, and $B$.  Applying
5222: the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}, to these recorded surfaces gives
5223: the stated current-package instantiation: each bounded case-study assertion
5224: obtains a finite certificate whose fields lie in $P$, the review bundle, or the
5225: explicit historical-evidence boundary.  The obstruction
5226: skeleton theorem then shows what a reviewer would have to find to reject any
5227: purported stronger reading: a missing path, missing gate row, missing promotion
5228: record, missing discovery-source row, or unsupported command-run escalation.
5229: Since $P$ records no command, environment, exit code, and log path for a fresh
5230: full-source rebuild, publication-daemon execution, or Rule110 dynamic rerun, and
5231: since Theorem~\ref{thm:verifier-input-output-contract} gives the verifier no
5232: output channel for fresh case-study rerun validity, the definition of command-run
5233: evidence prevents the corollary from asserting any of those stronger claims.\end{proof}
5234: 
5235: \section{Gate summary}
5236: 
5237: \subsection{Case-study witness protocol}
5238: 
5239: Table~\ref{tab:gates} lists the deterministic gates used by
5240: the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  The rows are operational
5241: interfaces: each gate has an evidence surface and a failure class it is meant
5242: to prevent.
5243: 
5244: \begin{table}
5245: \caption{Deterministic gate interfaces}
5246: \label{tab:gates}
5247: \small
5248: \begin{tabular}{p{0.23\linewidth}p{0.33\linewidth}p{0.32\linewidth}}
5249: \toprule
5250: Gate & Evidence surface & Failure prevented \\
5251: \midrule
5252: Formal-source gate & Lean build, axiom checks, axiom-purity audits & broken or impure formal targets \\
5253: Traceability gate & declaration inventory, source maps, marker audits & stale paper labels and missing source facts \\
5254: Discovery gate & certificate ledger, demotion, lineage DAG & statement-only, code-only, or mechanical ``discoveries'' \\
5255: Theorem-content delta gate & theorem inventory, phase-D hard lint, delta inventory & file churn or compilation reported as substantive theorem growth \\
5256: Artifact-limitation gate & status files, limitation ledgers, rerun logs when present & drift from bounded artifact evidence to stronger dynamic claims \\
5257: Scheduler gate & critical-path scoring and backlog windows & duplicated or random agent dispatch \\
5258: Promotion gate & active \texttt{2026\_*} directory plus pipeline metadata & intake seeds entering the daemon prematurely \\
5259: Overlap gate & route identity, semantic-overlap ledgers, submitted-sibling paths, board state & duplicate or racing paper routes \\
5260: Submission-state gate & submission markers, venue state, board state, submission metadata & invalid advancement of active or submitted routes \\
5261: Submission-pack gate & review, venue, bibliography, and metadata checks & unreviewed or under-specified submission packs \\
5262: \bottomrule
5263: \end{tabular}
5264: \end{table}
5265: 
5266: \begin{lemma}[Gate-witness criterion]
5267: \label{lem:gate-witness-criterion}
5268: A case record is a historical path-verified witness for the safety interface
5269: when it names the source or artifact snapshot surface, the invariant that failed,
5270: the gate decision recorded for that snapshot, and the safe manuscript lesson.
5271: Under the finite-record interface theorem,
5272: Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}, such a witness can support a
5273: case-study claim about the recorded historical gate surface, but not a stronger
5274: command-run, benchmark, live-daemon, rebuild, dynamic-artifact, or semantic
5275: validation claim, unless the corresponding command, source state, environment,
5276: exit code, and log path are also recorded.
5277: \end{lemma}
5278: 
5279: \begin{proof}
5280: The four named fields are exactly the data required by the definition of a
5281: path-verified historical evidence level: they identify the snapshot surface on
5282: which the case is checked, which gate predicate was evaluated, what decision was
5283: recorded, and which bounded claim may be carried into the manuscript.  A live
5284: benchmark, daemon execution, full-source rebuild, dynamic artifact run, or
5285: semantic validator would add an event time, command, source state, environment,
5286: exit code, log path, and usually a new artifact-output surface.  Those fields are
5287: not read by a historical witness.  Therefore a witness record with only the four
5288: path-verified fields supports the bounded case-study claim and cannot be used as
5289: evidence for a fresh command-run assertion.\end{proof}
5290: 
5291: \begin{proposition}[Path-complete case witnesses]
5292: \label{prop:path-complete-case-witnesses}
5293: Suppose a case-study row is used as load-bearing evidence for
5294: the finite-record interface theorem, Theorem~\ref{thm:publication-safety-interface}.  If the row is path-complete in
5295: the sense above, then the row supplies exactly the evidence surface required for
5296: a path-verified historical snapshot case claim and no evidence surface for a
5297: fresh daemon, full-source, theorem-content, artifact-suite, benchmark, or
5298: semantic-substrate rerun.  In fact every accepted path-complete case row factors
5299: through one of four finite witness skeletons---promotion, route/submission
5300: blocking, theorem-content non-growth, or artifact-limitation disclosure---and its
5301: admissible manuscript lesson is the unique bounded lesson attached to that
5302: skeleton.  Replacing that lesson by a fresh experiment, dynamic validation, live
5303: benchmark, or semantic artifact claim changes the skeleton by adding a
5304: command-run or artifact-semantic coordinate, so the original row no longer
5305: certifies the stronger claim.  In
5306: particular, a promotion row is sufficient only
5307: for the bounded claim that an intake packet is not daemon-visible publication
5308: work before human promotion; a route-overlap row is sufficient only for the
5309: bounded claim that the overlap and submission-state gates blocked advancement
5310: until one of the recorded next actions occurs; a theorem-content row is
5311: sufficient only for the bounded claim that file churn or compilation did not
5312: show substantive theorem growth; and an artifact-limitation row is sufficient
5313: only for the bounded claim that the artifact limitation must be disclosed or must
5314: block promotion.
5315: \end{proposition}
5316: 
5317: \begin{proof}
5318: Let $r$ be a path-complete case row.  By definition, every load-bearing
5319: component of $r$ has a concrete source or artifact snapshot path, directory
5320: manifest, or explicit historical boundary.  The promotion interface names the
5321: candidate surface, human-promotion evidence, active-paper
5322: markers, gate decision, and the bounded manuscript claim; these fields are
5323: precisely the data needed to distinguish inactive intake from publication work.
5324: The route-overlap interface names the active route, the submitted sibling that
5325: creates the chronology constraint, the reason for overlap, the gate decision,
5326: and the finite set of permitted next actions.  These are precisely the data
5327: needed to check whether advancement is allowed without appealing to generated
5328: prose, and the submission-state evidence prevents a route from racing an already
5329: submitted sibling.  The theorem-content interface names the changed surface,
5330: the theorem inventory or hard-lint surface, the substantive-content delta, the
5331: gate decision, and the allowed manuscript claim; these fields are precisely the
5332: data needed to reject extension claims based only on file churn or successful
5333: compilation.  The artifact-limitation interface names the status file, the
5334: limitation ledger, the observed limitation, the gate decision, and the only
5335: manuscript claim that may be carried forward.  These are precisely the data
5336: needed to prevent a failed or bounded artifact check from being promoted into a
5337: stronger dynamic-validation claim.  Lemma~\ref{lem:gate-witness-criterion} then
5338: applies to each such row:
5339: the named paths give the source surface, the interface fields give the failed
5340: invariant and decision, and the last field gives the safe lesson.  The same
5341: lemma also rules out upgrading the row to a command-run claim unless the extra
5342: command-run fields are recorded.  In particular, the proof does not rerun the
5343: publication daemon, overlap scanner, theorem-content detector, artifact suite,
5344: or GroundCompiler evaluator; it proves only that the historical path surfaces are
5345: sufficient for the bounded lessons displayed in the table.
5346: 
5347: It remains to justify the skeleton and uniqueness assertions.  The operational
5348: interface dispatches each case row by its gate family.  A row whose required gate
5349: is promotion has exactly the promotion skeleton; a row whose required gates are
5350: overlap and submission-state has the route/submission-blocking skeleton; a row
5351: whose required gate is theorem-content has the non-growth skeleton; and a row
5352: whose required gates are status and limitation-ledger has the artifact-limitation
5353: skeleton.  These four skeletons are disjoint because their gate sets differ, and
5354: the row's safe-lesson field is part of the finite record checked by
5355: Lemma~\ref{lem:gate-witness-criterion}.  Hence, once the skeleton is fixed, the
5356: only accepted lesson is the bounded lesson printed in that row.  A fresh
5357: experiment or dynamic validation would require the command-run boundary fields in
5358: Definition~\ref{def:operational-acceptance-interface}; an artifact-semantic claim
5359: would require an additional artifact pass record or semantic evaluator surface.
5360: Those coordinates are not read by the path-complete row and are not present in
5361: the four skeletons.  The stronger reading is therefore rejected by
5362: Theorem~\ref{thm:finite-coordinate-determination-boundary} together with the
5363: finite obstruction skeleton, while the original bounded historical lesson remains
5364: accepted.\end{proof}
5365: 
