5606: \url{https://www.springer.com/gp/computer-science/lncs/conference-proceedings-guidelines}.
5607: The local checks recorded HTTP status 200 for all three pages in the run witness
5608: \path{VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log} and in the later live-check witness
5609: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log}, with exit code 0, and observed the same route
5610: facts as the 2026-06-03 near-submission check: presentation-only papers are
5611: work-in-progress submissions of two pages plus bibliography, receive a
5612: light-weight review, do not appear in the Springer proceedings, have a
5613: 2026-06-15 submission deadline, and use the EasyChair/LNCS submission interface
5614: unless the final form gives a different instruction.  These facts are inputs to
5615: a local submission-pack readiness check only; if upload occurs after this check
5616: or the form shows a conflicting instruction, the finite venue gate must be run
5617: again and, if venue compliance is to be certified inside the submitted package,
5618: the updated venue record and log must be included in the submitted support
5619: surface.  Otherwise these file names record historical local readiness only.
5620: 
5621: \begin{proposition}[Fresh venue-record criterion]
5622: \label{audit:fresh-venue-record-criterion}
5623: Assume that, immediately before the actual upload action or at a time explicitly
5624: recorded as unchanged for that action, the final submitted support surface
5625: contains either the venue-check record \path{VENUE_CHECK.md} and log
5626: \path{VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log}, the later local-date rerun log
5627: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log}, or an
5628: archive-equivalent replacement naming the same checked URLs, observation time,
5629: route rules, command result, source state, environment, exit code, and log path.
5630: Then the venue row of Proposition~\ref{audit:venue-submission-pack-gate} is
5631: accepted for the current package only when the upload is made on that checked
5632: rule state or after a later record with the same fields has replaced it.  If
5633: that support surface is not submitted, or if an upload occurs after a venue-page
5634: change without a replacement record, the package retains only a dated local
5635: readiness observation and cannot certify upload-time venue compliance.
5636: 
5637: If the local venue-check files are not part of the submitted support surface,
5638: mentions of \path{VENUE_CHECK.md}, \path{VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log}, and
5639: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log} in
5640: this supplement are historical/path-verified diagnostic context only, not finite
5641: package coordinates for a venue certificate.
5642: \end{proposition}
5643: 
5644: \begin{proof}
5645: The venue gate uses facts that are external to the manuscript: route class,
5646: length, review status, proceedings boundary, deadline, submission form, style
5647: interface, and software/data-access instruction.  These facts can change outside
5648: the submitted source, so the gate cannot be discharged by a stale table row.
5649: The stated support-surface hypothesis supplies the finite certificate surface:
5650: three official URLs, a date and time, command-result fields, an HTTP-status run
5651: log, observed route facts, and the boundary that a later upload or conflicting
5652: form instruction triggers re-verification.  If the
5653: upload uses that recorded rule state, each venue-dependent row of
5654: Table~\ref{tab:venue-submission-pack-gate} is checked against a dated official
5655: surface.  If the upload occurs after a change, or without a replacement record,
5656: at least one external premise of Proposition~\ref{audit:venue-submission-pack-gate}
5657: is no longer certified by the package; the venue row is therefore not accepted.
5658: This proves the criterion and connects the fresh record to the local readiness
5659: gate.  Without the support-surface hypothesis, the named local files are not
5660: reviewer-available finite coordinates, so the same text can witness only a dated
5661: historical observation.
5662: \end{proof}
5663: 
5664: \begin{theorem}[Venue-rule freshness non-escalation]
5665: \label{thm:venue-rule-freshness-non-escalation}
5666: Let $U$ be the finite dated venue record consisting of the official call
5667: URL, the submission-form URL, the style-guideline URL, the observation date and
5668: time, the HTTP-status run witness \path{VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log} or the later rerun witness
5669: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log}, the
5670: observed route class, page limit, proceedings boundary, deadline, supplement
5671: access rule, and the local witness rows in Table~\ref{tab:venue-submission-pack-gate}.
5672: The venue component of the current finite-record package is accepted exactly for
5673: uploads whose venue-rule state is represented by $U$ or by a later replacement
5674: record with the same fields and with observation time immediately before upload,
5675: or with a finite unchanged-rule bridge from the recorded check to the upload
5676: action.  If an upload is made after a venue-page change, or if no upload-time or
5677: unchanged-rule replacement record is supplied, then the package retains only a
5678: historical venue observation and cannot certify submission-pack readiness,
5679: EasyChair compliance, acceptance, or proceedings status.
5680: \end{theorem}
5681: 
5682: \begin{proof}
5683: The venue rows used by the package are not internal mathematical definitions;
5684: they are external facts read from the official call, submission, and style
5685: surfaces.  Therefore the finite information available to the package about the
5686: venue is precisely the tuple $U$ displayed in the statement: three source URLs,
5687: one date and time, the HTTP-status run log, the finite route facts observed at
5688: that check, and the corresponding local witness rows.  On the class of uploads
5689: whose venue-rule state is represented by $U$, each premise of the local readiness gate is a component of that tuple, so
5690: Proposition~\ref{audit:fresh-venue-record-criterion} and
5691: Table~\ref{tab:venue-submission-pack-gate} determine the bounded readiness
5692: conclusion.
5693: 
5694: Now suppose the venue page changes before upload or the upload is made without a
5695: replacement record.  At least one external premise--route class, page limit,
5696: deadline, submission interface, proceedings boundary, or supplement rule--is then
5697: not determined by $U$.  Two possible upload states can agree on the historical
5698: record $U$ while differing on that changed premise.  A certificate that is a
5699: function only of $U$ cannot distinguish those two states, so it cannot certify the
5700: stronger upload-time claim.  A later replacement record with the same fields is
5701: exactly the finite enlargement needed to restore determinacy.  The excluded
5702: claims of EasyChair compliance, acceptance, and proceedings status require still
5703: more external records and are not fields of $U$.  Hence stale venue observations
5704: remain historical only, while the accepted venue gate is the fresh finite-record
5705: one stated above.
5706: \end{proof}
5707: 
5708: \begin{corollary}[Historical venue record non-escalation]
5709: \label{cor:historical-venue-record-non-escalation}
5710: The venue check recorded at \path{VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log}, with local
5711: observation time \path{2026-06-04 10:15 Asia/Singapore}, is a historical venue
5712: record.  For the present post-2026-06-04 source state it is superseded, for local
5713: readiness only, by the rerun log
5714: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log} and its companion record
5715: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.md}, whose local
5716: observation time and exit code are the fields printed in those files.  Neither
5717: dated record certifies actual upload-time EasyChair
5718: compliance, acceptance, or proceedings status unless the final submitted support
5719: surface also contains either an upload-time record with the same fields or an
5720: explicit statement that the upload used the unchanged venue-rule state represented
5721: by the latest dated record.
5722: \end{corollary}
5723: 
5724: \begin{proof}
5725: Apply Theorem~\ref{thm:venue-rule-freshness-non-escalation} first to the dated
5726: tuple whose HTTP-status witness is \path{VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log}.  The
5727: 2026-06-09 live-check log has the same required fields and is therefore the
5728: later replacement record for local readiness after the source has moved past
5729: 2026-06-04.  Applying the theorem to that latest tuple gives exactly the stated
5730: boundary: the package has a fresh local-readiness observation, but if the final
5731: support surface contains neither an upload-time replacement nor a statement tying
5732: the upload to the unchanged rule state represented by the latest tuple, then the
5733: upload-time venue-rule state is not a finite coordinate of the package.
5734: EasyChair compliance, acceptance, and proceedings status still require external
5735: records not present in either dated tuple.
5736: \end{proof}
5737: 
5738: \begin{corollary}[Upload-time venue-compliance record requirement]
5739: \label{cor:upload-time-venue-compliance-record-requirement}
5740: The logs \path{VENUE_CHECK_RUN_2026-06-04.log} and
5741: \path{review_bundle/VENUE_BIBLIOGRAPHY_LIVE_CHECK_2026-06-09.log} are dated
5742: local-readiness records.  For the current package they certify only the venue
5743: rule state observed at their recorded observation times.  The current source
5744: package contains no EasyChair upload receipt, no completed-upload timestamp, and
5745: no finite statement tying a completed upload to the unchanged venue-rule state;
5746: the public branch/path archive-equivalent locator is a support-surface locator,
5747: not an upload-time venue-compliance record.  Consequently these logs do not
5748: certify upload-time EasyChair compliance.  Such a certification would require a
5749: future submitted support surface to contain either
5750: \begin{enumerate}
5751: \item a later upload-time venue/bibliography record with the same URL,
5752: observation-time, command-result, source-state, environment, exit-code, and
5753: log-path fields; or
5754: \item a finite statement that the completed upload used the unchanged venue-rule
5755: state represented by the latest included dated record.
5756: \end{enumerate}
5757: In the present package neither record is present, so all venue-dependent conclusions in
5758: Proposition~\ref{audit:venue-submission-pack-gate} and
5759: Table~\ref{tab:venue-submission-pack-gate} remain historical local-readiness
5760: claims and cannot be escalated to upload-time compliance, acceptance, or
5761: proceedings-status claims.
5762: \end{corollary}
5763: 
5764: \begin{proof}
5765: Theorem~\ref{thm:venue-rule-freshness-non-escalation} identifies the finite venue
5766: record $U$ by its official URLs, observation time, run witness, observed route
5767: facts, and witness rows.  The two named logs instantiate such records at their
5768: own dated observation times.  A final upload-time compliance claim, however,
5769: depends on an external state not contained in those dated logs unless the upload
5770: is explicitly tied to the same unchanged rule state or a later replacement record
5771: is supplied.
5772: 
5773: The present source package includes only the two dated local-readiness logs.  It
5774: does not include a later upload-time tuple and does not include a statement that
5775: a completed upload used the unchanged rule state represented by the latest dated
5776: tuple.  Therefore two upload states can agree with all bytes of the current
5777: package while differing on the live venue rule, submission form, deadline, or
5778: supplement-access instruction.  A certificate depending only on the present
5779: package cannot distinguish those states.  By the finite-coordinate boundary, the
5780: stronger upload-time, acceptance, and proceedings conclusions therefore do not
5781: follow from the current logs.  If a future package adds one of the two listed
5782: records, that added finite coordinate is precisely the new premise needed to
5783: re-run Proposition~\ref{audit:venue-submission-pack-gate}; it is not a coordinate
5784: claimed here.
5785: \end{proof}
5786: 
